            "text": "**Fossilized poop is called a _coprolite_.**\n\nCoprolites can be very useful to paleontologists because they may contain clues about an animal\u2019s diet, digestion, parasites, gut bacteria, and environment. For example, bits of bone, scales, plant material, pollen, or shells inside a coprolite can show what the animal ate.\n\nThey can come from dinosaurs, ancient fish, reptiles, mammals, or even humans. Despite being poop, once fossilized they are essentially rock.",
